    "word": "petiole",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                "word": "petiole",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6ee787d0-0df0-4c85-8f8c-11fb2d1e1bb5",
                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "petioles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The stalk of a leaf, attaching the blade to the stem."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b826f04-e29c-41e0-8266-aab98b83f83f",
                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                "text": "Most insects consume tissue from the leaf blade were measured just past the twist on the side away only, leaving the leaf petioles unscathed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7e88fd8-7dcf-4eb4-9265-9b6e27ab80d7",
                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                "text": "By contrast, the petioles of large pinnate leaves, as well as stems, typically resist torsion by placing stiff materials with high elastic moduli (like sclerenchyma) toward the perimeters of their cross sections."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeaa8590-d081-4714-816f-dbeaf21e06d8",
                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                "text": "An example of this is leaf petioles. Some species of trees have pinnate leaves which, when the leaves fall, shed pinnae from the petiole, which is then left as a tapering, somewhat flexible rod."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a2ee98b-32d9-33f1-8c42-70d8a87fa550",
                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A narrow or constricted segment of the body of an insect; especially, the metasomal segment of certain Hymenoptera, such as wasps."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee91132e-51e0-3d17-84a9-eae23d3cccec",
                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The stalk at the base of the nest of the paper wasp."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
